   "source": [
    "# Converting the 'User_Score' column to numeric while handling non-numerical entries\n",
    "df['User_Score'] = pd.to_numeric(\n",
    "    df['User_Score'], \n",
    "    errors='coerce' # Convert non-numerical entries to NaN\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "median_user_score = df['User_Score'].median()\n",
    "df['User_Score'] = df['User_Score'].fillna(median_user_score)\n",
    "df"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7885921b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "> Although this approach replaces missing user scores with the median, it does cloud true user preferences and may not accurately reflect the original distribution of user scores. For example, `Super Mario Bros.` may have had no user score originally, but now it appears to have the median user score which may not reflect the actual sentiment of the users."
   ]
  }
 ],
